quation:\n\n$$\n0+\\frac{1}{60}\\alpha =0.6\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =36.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is ${Q}_{p}(t)=36.$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\nQ(t)={Q}_{c}(t)+{Q}_{p}(t)=A{e}^{-t/60}+36.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the vat initially contains $25\\,\\text{kg}$ of dissolved dye. So, we can apply the initial condition $Q(0)=25,$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(0) & =25 \\\\ A{e}^{-0/60}+36 & =25 \\\\ A & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following expression for $Q(t):$\n\n$$\nQ(t)=36-11{e}^{-t/60}\n$$\n\nFinally,  the amount of dye in the vat $6$ minutes after pumping begins is\n\n$$\nQ(6)=36-11{e}^{-6/60}≈26.05\\,\\text{kg},\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."] [:db/cas 17592186557627 :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=- \\frac{5 t^{2}}{4} - \\frac{4 t}{3} - 6.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(2)=- \\frac{5 (2)^{2}}{4} - \\frac{4 (2)}{3} - 6=(-6)+(-5)+\\left(- \\frac{8}{3}\\right)=- \\frac{41}{3}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=- \\frac{3 t^{2}}{4} - \\frac{t}{3} + 6.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(3)=- \\frac{3 (3)^{2}}{4} - \\frac{(3)}{3} + 6=(6)+\\left(- \\frac{27}{4}\\right)+(-1)=- \\frac{7}{4}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $x(4),$ we substitute $t=4$ into $x=- \\frac{5 t^{2}}{4} - \\frac{4 t}{3} - 6.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(4)=- \\frac{5 (4)^{2}}{4} - \\frac{4 (4)}{3} - 6=(-6)+(-20)+\\left(- \\frac{16}{3}\\right)=- \\frac{94}{3}.\n$$\n\nThen the table is\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $- \\frac{103}{12}$ | $- \\frac{41}{3}$ | $- \\frac{85}{4}$ | $- \\frac{94}{3}$ | $- \\frac{527}{12}$ |\n| $y$ | $6$ | $\\frac{59}{12}$ | $\\frac{7}{3}$ | $- \\frac{7}{4}$ | $- \\frac{22}{3}$ | $- \\frac{173}{12}$ |" "- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $$\n\